<title>ITALY: Italy's Florence sees Feb CPI at -0.1 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Florence sees Feb CPI at -0.1 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>FLORENCE, Italy 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Florence said its February consumer price index stood at -0.1 percent month-on-month and 2.0 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In January, Florence's inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 2.2 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Florence is one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 6.08 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to January 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		    -0.1   (0.1)     2.0  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.2  (-0.7)     0.7  (1.5)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.1   (0.1)     2.7  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -1.6  (0.5)	2.1  (4.0)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.1   (0.0)     2.2  (2.3)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.1   (1.9)     2.5  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.0  (-0.7)     1.0  (1.0)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.1  (-0.5)     1.9 (-0.5)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.9   (0.0)     4.9  (3.8)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	 -0.2   (1.7)     4.6  (5.2)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.1   (0.0)     1.0  (1.5)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
